## Lite-ESRGAN

Lite-ESRGAN: High-Quality Super-Resolution for Everyone. A streamlined, low-VRAM implementation of the Real-ESRGAN model.

### Structure
- `src/utils.py`: Image I/O, degradations, resize helpers, tensor conversions, device utils, model save/load, and a prefetching dataloader.
- `src/dataset.py`: `ImageDataset` for paired LR/HR samples with realistic degradations.
- `src/model.py`: `SRNet` (generator), `VGGNet` (perceptual features), `Discriminator` (GAN stage).
- `src/train_base.py`: Stage 1 training (pixel + perceptual loss).
- `src/train_gan.py`: Stage 2 training (adds GAN loss).
- `src/inference.py`: Load a trained model and upscale an image.

### Install
```bash
pip install .
```

### Datasets
Place training images under `data/` (or adjust the path inside training scripts).

Put a sample image `sample.png` under `test_data`. For every hundreds of steps, an upscaled sample data will be generated for evaluation.

### Train

Training can be done on a 4GB GPU. If you have a better GPU, increase `batch_size` to get better result.

- Stage 1:
```bash
python src/train_base.py
```
- Stage 2:
```bash
python src/train_gan.py
```

Models and test outputs are saved under `./model_base`, `./model_gan`, `./test_base`, and `./test_gan` per script settings.

### Inference

On a 4GB GPU, the original Real-ESRGAN can handle up to about 300x300 image patch at a time, while this Lite-ESRGAN can handle about 1000x1000 image patch.

Edit `src/inference.py` to set the input image path, then:
```bash
python src/inference.py
```

